# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in only what you need. Nothing here is needed for the
# default flow: `make e2e-env-up && make e2e` runs against the local compose stack and the fake
# Google, with no secrets. Variables already set in the shell win.

# Mattermost under test. Defaults to the compose stack on localhost:8075 (SiteURL must be a
# redirect URI the OAuth client allows).
# PW_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8075
# The suite logs in as this system admin (created automatically on an empty server).
# PW_ADMIN_USERNAME=sysadmin
# PW_ADMIN_PASSWORD=Sys@dmin-sample1
# The suite deletes plugin data and rewrites plugin settings on its target, so it refuses a
# PW_BASE_URL, E2E_DATABASE_URL or FAKE_GOOGLE_URL that isn't localhost (lib/safety.ts). Set this
# only for a disposable remote test server.
# E2E_ALLOW_REMOTE_SERVER=1

# Compose stack image and host ports (docker-compose.yml). docker compose does not read this file:
# these are shell exports for `make e2e-env-up`, as script/visual.sh sets them, e.g.
#   MM_PORT=8076 E2E_DB_PORT=5435 E2E_FAKE_PORT=8092 E2E_FAKE_HTTPS_PORT=8455 make e2e-env-up
# The image is amd64-only; on Apple silicon Docker Desktop runs it under Rosetta.
#   MM_IMAGE=mattermost/mattermost-enterprise-edition:12.0
#   MM_PORT=8075 E2E_DB_PORT=5434 E2E_FAKE_PORT=8090 E2E_FAKE_HTTPS_PORT=8453
# If you change a port, point the suite at it too (here or in the shell), all together:
# PW_BASE_URL (MM_PORT), E2E_DATABASE_URL (E2E_DB_PORT), FAKE_GOOGLE_URL (E2E_FAKE_PORT) and
# E2E_FAKE_HTTPS_PORT, which lib/browser.ts also reads to route Google's hostnames to the fake.
# E2E_FAKE_HTTPS_PORT=8453
# E2E_DATABASE_URL=postgres://mmuser:mostest@127.0.0.1:5434/mattermost_test
# FAKE_GOOGLE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8090

# Which Google the run talks to: fake (default; fake-google/ in the compose stack, no accounts or
# secrets) or real (the accounts below; start the stack with `make e2e-env-up E2E_GOOGLE=real`).
# `npm run test:real` sets real. The real lane runs locally only; it is not in CI yet.
# E2E_GOOGLE=fake

# Real Google only. OAuth client the plugin is configured with; register
# http://localhost:8075/plugins/com.mattermost.gcal/oauth2/complete and
# http://localhost:8765/callback as redirect URIs.
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# refresh_token (local Gmail, from `npm run google:auth -- owner|collab`) or dwd (Workspace, not implemented).
# GOOGLE_AUTH_MODE=refresh_token
# GOOGLE_OWNER_EMAIL=
# GOOGLE_OWNER_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# GOOGLE_COLLAB_EMAIL=
# GOOGLE_COLLAB_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# Required on real Google: the accounts above must be listed here (comma-separated addresses, or
# @domain for the Workspace test org). The real lane creates events on them and sends them invites,
# and google:auth refuses any other account.
# E2E_GOOGLE_TEST_ACCOUNTS=owner@example.com,collab@example.com
